# Getting commits onto STAGE (full process — I keep forgetting the deploy step)

"Push to stage" = **promote the branch AND rebuild the container on the box.**
A `git push origin stage` alone changes nothing that's live. Two steps, always.

## 1. Promote `main` → `stage` (fast-forward only, PowerShell: use `;` never `&&`)

```powershell
git checkout stage; git merge --ff-only main; git push origin stage; git checkout main
```

- Commit + push work to `main` first. Never commit straight onto `stage`.
- If `--ff-only` is rejected, `stage` has commits `main` lacks — reconcile on
  `main`, never force-push an environment branch.

## 2. Deploy on the stage box (I HAVE SSH ACCESS — always run this)

Stage is containerized Docker Compose at `10.90.15.6`; `/code` is a checkout of
the `stage` branch. Pull the release into it and rebuild the image:

```powershell
ssh dmadmin@10.90.15.6 'git -C /home/dmadmin/docker-staging/qtip-app/code pull --ff-only; cd /home/dmadmin/docker-staging/qtip-app; docker compose up -d --build'
```

- **`.env`-only change** (no code): `docker compose up -d` (no `--build`).
- **DB migration** in the release: apply it before the rebuild (runbook §3.3).

## 3. Verify

Load `https://qtip-stage.dm.local` (self-signed cert prompt is expected). Confirm
the box HEAD matches origin: `ssh dmadmin@10.90.15.6 'git -C /home/dmadmin/docker-staging/qtip-app/code rev-parse HEAD'`.

Full reference: `docs/deployment_runbook.md` §0a/§0b. Prod (`10.90.15.5`) is a
separate promote+deploy and is NEVER done automatically — verify stage first.
